.Dd September 14, 2026
.Dt ANOINT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm anoint
.Nd run a command holding one additional anointment
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Ar name
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility runs
.Ar command
with the calling session's capability reach extended by exactly one
anointment,
.Ar name ,
after the caller re-enters its own password.
It is the capability system's replacement for
.Xr sudo 8
and
.Xr doas 1 :
elevation shaped as least privilege.
.Pp
.Nm
never changes the user id.
.Ar command
runs as the caller, with the caller's environment and working directory;
what changes is only the set of anointments carried by the ambient
lookup channel
.Ar command
inherits, which is the session's own set plus
.Ar name .
A capability service whose endpoint
.Em requires
.Ar name
therefore becomes reachable for that one command, and for nothing else the
caller runs.
When
.Ar command
exits the elevated channel is gone; a further
.Nm
authenticates again.
Nothing is cached and there is no timeout window.
.Pp
Whether a principal may elevate to
.Ar name
at all is decided by the
.Cm may_elevate
list of its entry in
.Pa /Capabilities/Config/principal-policy.ucl
.Pq see Xr authagentd 8 .
A name outside that list is refused before any password prompt.
Every request, granted or refused, is audited by
.Xr authagentd 8
with the caller's uid, session label and the requested name.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl n
Do not prompt; send an empty password.
Useful only from scripts for an account whose stored password is empty;
an account with no usable password
.Pq an empty or locked hash
is refused regardless.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
requires a session: it must be run from a login session, an
.Xr ssh 1
session or an
.Xr su 1
shell that carries an ambient lookup channel.
It talks to
.Dq Li system.authagent
directly over that channel; no set-user-id binary and no
.Xr sudoers 5 Ns -style
file is involved, and the authentication happens inside the agent's
sandbox against
.Pa /etc/master.passwd ,
not through PAM.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 when it refuses to run
.Ar command :
the name is not permitted for this principal, the password was wrong, too
many recent failures were recorded for this user, there is no session
channel, or the agent could not be reached.
It exits 126 when
.Ar command
was found but could not be executed and 127 when it could not be found.
Otherwise the exit status is that of
.Ar command .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Publish a system notification on the gated tier of
.Sy system.Notify
.Pq Fl s ,
which requires
.Dq Li system.notify.system :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ anoint system.notify.system notifyctl -s publish system.maint "reboot at 02:00"
Password:
.Ed
.Pp
Restart a managed service, gated on
.Dq Li system.switchboard.admin :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ anoint system.switchboard.admin switchboardctl restart system.Network
.Ed
.Pp
The corresponding principal-policy entry that permits the first example
for members of
.Dq operators :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
principals {
    operators {
        groups = ["operators"];
        anointments = ["system.trace.client"];
        may_elevate = ["system.notify.system"];
    }
}
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "anoint: not permitted"
The caller's principal entry does not list
.Ar name
.Pq or Dq Li * Ns
in
.Cm may_elevate .
No password was asked for.
.It "anoint: authentication failed"
The password did not match.
.It "anoint: too many failures"
Five failed attempts within a minute for this user; wait and retry.
.It "anoint: session already holds the maximum number of anointments"
The principal's policy set is full and
.Ar name
is not already in it, so no channel could be minted
.Pq Er E2BIG .
.It "anoint: no session channel"
The calling process carries no ambient lookup channel and so is not part
of a session.
.It "anoint: auth agent unavailable"
.Xr authagentd 8
is not registered with
.Xr switchboard 8
.Pq Er ENOENT .
.It "anoint: auth agent did not answer"
The agent did not reply within five seconds
.Pq Er ETIMEDOUT .
.It "anoint: elevation is not enabled on this system"
The agent was not granted
.Pa /etc/master.passwd
and cannot authenticate anyone
.Pq Er ENXIO .
.It "anoint: auth agent rejected the request"
The agent found the request malformed
.Pq Er EINVAL ,
which indicates a library/agent version mismatch.
.It "anoint: malformed reply from auth agent"
The reply did not have the expected shape
.Pq Er EBADMSG .
.El
.Pp
Every outcome is also recorded by the agent in the audit trail
.Pq Dv AUE_AUTHAGENT_ELEVATE
and to
.Dv LOG_AUTHPRIV ;
see
.Xr authagentd 8 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr authagentd 8 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Fx 5BSD
as part of IPC anointments.
Unlike
.Xr sudo 8
and
.Xr doas 1
it grants a named capability rather than a user id.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
